From 3a9f1f2dfad4c9eae9e46cf43f00355889fb7542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olaoluwa Osuntokun <laolu32@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:54:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] compiler: make cache output reproducible

In this commit, we serialize unordered cache collections in key order and stabilize the traversal that allocates imported type IDs. Equal module interfaces, diagnostic names, Unicode source mappings, and local package manifests can otherwise produce different bytes between clean builds.

We preserve the existing serde wire shapes and runtime hash randomization. The regression tests cover equivalent maps and sets, type-ID remapping, diagnostic names, and Git package state.

This is the Gleam 1.18.1 patch rebased onto v1.19.0-rc2. That release removed the inlining pass, so the inline parameter list and the decision-tree label map are no longer serialized, and their ordering and regression test were dropped. The line-number mapping moved to the src-span crate, which now carries its own ordered serializer, and the cache format moved from bincode to bitcode, which writes maps in iteration order just as bincode did.
